      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Depigmented skin patches"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports increased white patches over 6–9 months, especially the last 3 months, on the hands, peri-oral area, and a small peri-ocular area. Patches are described as completely white and well-defined; more obvious since increased sun exposure. Examination: multiple sharply demarcated depigmented macules/patches on the dorsum of the hands, peri-oral 'milk moustache' area, small eyelid patches, and older patches on the ankles/feet. No scale or erythema. Some follicular repigmentation on older ankle lesions and a few white hairs in lesions. No obvious dermatitis."
      }
    },
